{"name":"Valley of Tears","hex":"#d1e1e4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"valley","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elongated depression cast between hills or mountains, often with a river flowing through it.","An area which drains itself into a river."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form the shape of a valley."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valley"},{"term":"tears","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of tear (“liquid from the eyes”)","Viscous streaks left on the inside of the glass when certain wines are swirled around before tasting."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of tear"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tears"}],"entries":[{"title":"Valley of Tears","blocks":[{"text":"The Valley of Tears is the name given to an area in the Golan Heights after it became the site of a major battle in 1973 during the Yom Kippur War, known as the Valley of Tears Battle, which was fought from 6 October to 9 October. Although massively outnumbered, the Israeli forces managed to hold their positions and on the fourth day of the battle the Syrians withdrew, just as the Israeli defences were almost at the point of collapse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Destroyed_Syrian_T-62_with_Fallen_Crew_Member_Somewhere_in_the_Golan_Sector%2C_Yom_Kippur_War%2C_8_October_1973.jpg/330px-Destroyed_Syrian_T-62_with_Fallen_Crew_Member_Somewhere_in_the_Golan_Sector%2C_Yom_Kippur_War%2C_8_October_1973.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_of_Tears"},{"title":"Valley of Tears (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Valley of Tears, is an Israeli television miniseries directed by Yaron Zilberman based on a screenplay by Ron Leshem and Daniel Amsel and starring Aviv Alush, Joy Rieger, and Lior Ashkenazi. Development of the series lasted about a decade and its filming took place over 52 days starting on July 21, 2019. The premiere episode of the first season aired on Kan 11 on October 19, 2020. It was subsequently licensed by HBO Max, airing on November 12, 2020."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/06/Valley_of_Tears_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_of_Tears_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Valley","blocks":[{"text":"A valley is an elongated low area often running between hills or mountains and typically containing a river or stream running from one end to the other. Most valleys are formed by erosion of the land surface by rivers or streams over a very long period. Some valleys are formed through erosion by glacial ice. These glaciers may remain present in valleys in high mountains or polar areas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG/330px-Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley"},{"title":"Tears","blocks":[{"text":"Tears are a transparent fluid secreted primarily by the lacrimal glands found in the eyes of all land mammals. According to the mode of production, tears are classified into four types: basal, closed eye, emotional, and reflex. The basal rate of tear secretion is ~0.5–2.2 μL/min, and irritation can increase secretion by up to ~100-fold, reaching ~300 μL/min. Tears are made up of water, electrolytes, proteins, lipids, and mucins that form layers on the surface of eyes. The four types of tears differ significantly in their composition."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/USMC-04952.jpg/330px-USMC-04952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tears"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Shot_Kal-.jpg/500px-Shot_Kal-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Shot_Kal-.jpg/500px-Shot_Kal-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Israeli Sho't Kal, an upgraded Centurion tank","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShot_Kal-.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/The_Bloody_Valley_of_Tears_Battle_-_Flickr_-_Israel_Defense_Forces.jpg/500px-The_Bloody_Valley_of_Tears_Battle_-_Flickr_-_Israel_Defense_Forces.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/The_Bloody_Valley_of_Tears_Battle_-_Flickr_-_Israel_Defense_Forces.jpg/500px-The_Bloody_Valley_of_Tears_Battle_-_Flickr_-_Israel_Defense_Forces.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Valley of Tears battle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Bloody_Valley_of_Tears_Battle_-_Flickr_-_Israel_Defense_Forces.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Valley_of_Tears.jpg/500px-Valley_of_Tears.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Valley_of_Tears.jpg/1280px-Valley_of_Tears.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Valley_of_Tears.jpg/500px-Valley_of_Tears.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Valley of Tears in 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AValley_of_Tears.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Syrian_Brigadier_General_of_the_7th_Inpantry_Division_Omar_Abrash%2C_killed_in_the_battle_of_the_%22Valley_of_Tears%22.jpg/500px-Syrian_Brigadier_General_of_